        <h2 id="final-thoughts">Final Thoughts</h2>
        <p>Google and AI assistants are scoring different things. Google scores the page, using links, query match and clicks. A model scores the passage, using context, entity clarity and what the rest of the web already says about you. The chart above is the shortest way I know to explain that split, and the biggest gaps on it are where your next quarter of work should go.</p>
        <p>I publish the test results behind these weightings, and revise them as the systems change, inside The New Search, my AI SEO community on Skool. If you want to see the pages that got cited and the ones that did not, that is where the evidence lives.</p>
